#>wonder_smut_crew_prose
?["Who writes the prose: the creator, a draft for the creator to edit, or text generated per visit?"]{
  ~#with: @plan
  ~#taste: "Authored scenes keep the voice the site was built on; generated text would vary every visit and answer to no one."
  ~#tension: "Daily variance asks for more pieces than one hand writes quickly; the draw can vary which authored pieces meet, not the sentences."
  !probe{ "rg -n 'body: \\[' workers/smut-today/src/index.js" }
}

#>wonder_smut_crew_assembly
?["Is putting a story together the reader's act, the creator's authoring tool, or both?"]{
  ~#with: @plan
  ~#taste: "The same slots can serve a reader choosing tonight and an author planning a season."
  ~#tension: "A reader tool wants few, legible choices; an authoring tool wants every facet at once."
  !probe{ "rg -n 'SETTLE' workers/smut-today/src/index.js" }
}

#>wonder_smut_crew_names
?["Does the crew get names, or roles only?"]{
  ~#with: @plan
  ~#taste: "Names make a village; roles keep everyone a composite."
  ~#tension: "A name is the first thing a real person could be read into; a role alone can feel like a cast list."
  !probe{ "rg -n 'pairing:' workers/smut-today/src/index.js" }
}

#>wonder_smut_crew_existing
?["Should the two stories, the letter and the shelf fold into the crew world, keep a hall of their own, or retire?"]{
  ~#with: @plan
  ~#taste: "What a returning reader already knows should land somewhere, not vanish."
  ~#tension: "The letter is addressed to one sitter, and that casting fell through; folding it in would re-address it."
  !probe{ "rg -n 'slug: "' workers/smut-today/src/index.js" }
}

#>wonder_smut_crew_limits
?["What are the hard limits for the crew world?"]{
  ~#with: @plan
  ~#taste: "A list set once, in the creator's words, lets every draft be checked against it."
  ~#tension: "Limits written by anyone else would be a guess about someone else's heat."
  !probe{ "rg -n 'Guards' .agents/plans/smut-today-crew/PLAN.md" }
}
